01:00:11,250 --> 01:00:17,250
Shirley is a 2020 American biographical drama film directed by Josephine Decker from a screenplay by Sarah Gubbins, based on the 2014 novel by Susan Scarf
Merrell, which formed a "largely fictional story" around novelist Shirley Jackson during the time period she was writing her 1951 novel Hangsaman.

10
01:06:52,500 --> 01:06:58,500
The film stars Elisabeth Moss as Jackson, with Michael Stuhlbarg,
Odessa Young, and Logan Lerman in supporting roles.

11
01:13:33,750 --> 01:13:39,750
Martin Scorsese serves as an executive producer.

12
01:20:15,000 --> 01:20:21,000
Shirley had its world premiere at the Sundance Film Festival on January 25, 2020,
where Decker won the Special Jury Award for Auteur Filmmaking.

13
01:26:56,250 --> 01:27:02,250
The film was released in the United States on June 5, 2020, to
positive reviews, with praise for Moss's performance.

14
01:33:37,500 --> 01:33:43,500
The film explores themes of husband wife relationship,
biography, writer, woman director, young couple.

